This has nothing to do with the locking problem. It sidesteps it. If
araizen (or whoever wants to do offline or more convient editing) does
a cvs up (or whatever it is with RCS), they can edit at their leisure
and then commit later. If the file has changed since they checked it
out you get to do normal merging (which is far more preferable than just
saying "no you can't edit this").

